    h2 Primitive Types§
    row
      link array primitive.array.html
      text A fixed-size array, denoted [T; N], for the element type, T, and the non-negative compile-time constant size, N.
      link bool primitive.bool.html
      text The boolean type.
      link char primitive.char.html
      text A character type.
      link f32 primitive.f32.html
      text A 32-bit floating-point type (specifically, the “binary32” type defined in IEEE 754-2008).
      link f64 primitive.f64.html
      text A 64-bit floating-point type (specifically, the “binary64” type defined in IEEE 754-2008).
      link fn primitive.fn.html
      text Function pointers, like fn(usize) -> bool.
      link i8 primitive.i8.html
      text The 8-bit signed integer type.
      link i16 primitive.i16.html
      text The 16-bit signed integer type.
      link i32 primitive.i32.html
      text The 32-bit signed integer type.
      link i64 primitive.i64.html
      text The 64-bit signed integer type.
      link i128 primitive.i128.html
      text The 128-bit signed integer type.
      link isize primitive.isize.html
      text The pointer-sized signed integer type.
      link pointer primitive.pointer.html
      text Raw, unsafe pointers, *const T, and *mut T.
      link reference primitive.reference.html
      text References, &T and &mut T.
      link slice primitive.slice.html
      text A dynamically-sized view into a contiguous sequence, [T].
      link str primitive.str.html
      text String slices.
      link tuple primitive.tuple.html
      text A finite heterogeneous sequence, (T, U, ..).
      link u8 primitive.u8.html
      text The 8-bit unsigned integer type.
      link u16 primitive.u16.html
      text The 16-bit unsigned integer type.
      link u32 primitive.u32.html
      text The 32-bit unsigned integer type.
      link u64 primitive.u64.html
      text The 64-bit unsigned integer type.
      link u128 primitive.u128.html
      text The 128-bit unsigned integer type.
      link unit primitive.unit.html
      text The () type, also called “unit”.
      link usize primitive.usize.html
      text The pointer-sized unsigned integer type.
