    h2 Attributes§
    row
      link allow attribute.allow.html
      text The  attribute suppresses lint diagnostics that would otherwise produce warnings or errors. It can be used on any lint or lint group (except those set to ).
      col
        text allow
        link forbid ./attribute.forbid.html
      link cfg attribute.cfg.html
      text Used for conditional compilation.
      link cold attribute.cold.html
      text Hint to the compiler that a function is unlikely to be called.
      link deny attribute.deny.html
      text Emits an error, preventing the compilation from finishing, when a lint check has failed. This is useful for enforcing rules or preventing certain patterns:
      link deprecated attribute.deprecated.html
      text Emits a warning during compilation when an item with this attribute is used. since and note are optional fields giving more detail about why the item is deprecated.
      link forbid attribute.forbid.html
      text Emits an error, preventing the compilation from finishing, when a lint check has failed.
      link inline attribute.inline.html
      text Suggest that the compiler inline a function at its call sites.
      link link_section attribute.link_section.html
      text Places a function or static in a specific object-file section.
      link must_use attribute.must_use.html
      text Warn when a value is ignored.
      link no_std attribute.no_std.html
      text Prevents automatically linking the standard library.
      link non_exhaustive attribute.non_exhaustive.html
      text Indicates that a type might have more fields or variants added in the future.
      link proc_macro attribute.proc_macro.html
      text Defines a function-like procedural macro.
      link track_caller attribute.track_caller.html
      text Make a function report the location of its caller instead of its own.
      link warn attribute.warn.html
      text Emits a warning during compilation when a lint check failed.
